<statement>
<p>
	This function is responsible for handling the player&#x27;s movement within the maze. The player's position is updated based on the input direction, provided the new location is not a wall. Additionally, this function handles the player&#x27;s collection of the key or torch if they move to its location.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>maze</pf> (struct) number — : The structure representing the maze. It includes all the fields described in <pf>HW4_initialize_game</pf>.</p>
			<p><pf>player</pf> (struct) number — - The structure representing the player's current state. It includes all the fields described in <pf>HW4_initialize_game</pf>.</p>
			<p><pf>direction</pf> (char) number — : The direction in which the player intends to move. It can be one of the following.</p>
			<p><pf>'w'</pf> number — : Move up.</p>
			<p><pf>'s'</pf> number — : Move down.</p>
			<p><pf>'a'</pf> number — : Move left.</p>
			<p><pf>'d'</pf> number — : Move right.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>player</pf> (struct) number — : The updated player structure reflects the new position, number of moves, and whether the key has been collected.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>If necessary, this function should update ALL of the fields of the player structure, including the sight.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>The</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>direction</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>field should be updated even if the player tries to move into a wall; however, the</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>moves</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>field should not.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
